    "title": "Dothan's Diggy Coleman commits to Arkansas State - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Christian Jones ,\n1 hours ago\nDOTHAN, Ala. ( WDHN )—One Circle City superstar is moving on from one wolfpack to another.\nOn Wednesday, it was revealed that Dothan Wolves point guard Diggy Coleman officially committed to the Arkansas State Red Wolves.\nFor Coleman, it seemed like love at first sight, given that he received his official offer from the school earlier in the week.\nThis latest accomplishment is the cherry on top of an already stellar senior year; one that saw him lead his team to a final four appearance, be named to the Alabama roster in the Alabama-Mississippi All-Star game, and be named as an ASWA First-Team All-State player and a 7A State Player of the Year finalist.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WDHN - wdhn.com.",
